; ..\BSW364\Com\Implementation\Com_RxProcessing.c	  2587       Reason:     All calls of the Com_ProcessRxFctPtrCacheFunction are directly or indirectly wraped by preprocessor switches checking if a FctPtrCache is available and the setting of the fctPtrCacheStrctPtr is wrapped by the same preprocessor switches, so the fctPtrCacheStrctPtr is always valid, when accessed.
; ..\BSW364\Com\Implementation\Com_RxProcessing.c	  2588       Risk:       No risk.
